# Collection & host-type combinations

Every Construction shape for **arrays** and **maps**, both **tagged**
(`[:Array/T …]`, `{K:V …}`) and **bare** (types inferred from the Schema slot),
plus ordinary Schema classes, **platform** values (via `%requires` CONSTRUCT),
and **`@` externals**.

Sigils attach to components, not to `[Array]` / `{Map}` elements. Platform
dates appear as bare `Date` in Schema once Target declares `CONSTRUCT`; the
external maths handle remains a root `@` factory argument.

Bare `{name:value}` with two Names is parsed as an empty typed map
(`Map<name,value>`), so Methods uses `{String:Int who:n}` for the rewrite.

## Schema

```
Person = String/name
Bundle =
  [String]/taggedStrings
  [String]/bareStrings
  [Person]/taggedPeople
  [Person]/barePeople
  {String:Int}/taggedScores
  {String:Int}/bareScores
  [Date]/taggedDates
  [Date]/bareDates
  {String:Date}/taggedByName
  {String:Date}/bareByName
  Date/founded
  @WCHNTMaths/maths
```

## Construction

```
ada = [:Person "Ada"].
bob = [:Person "Bob"].
d1815 = [:Date 1815 11 10 0 0 0].
d1970 = [:Date 1970 0 1 0 0 0].

[:Bundle
  [:Array/String "red" "green"]
  ["blue" "white"]
  [:Array/Person ada bob]
  [ada bob]
  {String:Int "Ada":3 "Bob":0}
  {"Cy":5 "Di":1}
  [:Array/Date d1815 d1970]
  [d1815 d1970]
  {String:Date "ada":d1815 "bob":d1970}
  {"cy":d1815 "di":d1970}
  d1815
  maths]
```

## Methods

```
Bundle::pi = { maths.sin(0) }

Bundle::relabel = { String/who, Int/n |
  [:Bundle
    taggedStrings
    bareStrings
    taggedPeople
    barePeople
    taggedScores
    {String:Int who:n}
    taggedDates
    bareDates
    taggedByName
    bareByName
    founded
    maths]
}
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%requires
Date
Date::CONSTRUCT(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) -> Date
Date::getFullYear() -> Int
WCHNTMaths::sin(Float) -> Float

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    var b = BundleAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths);
    wchntConsole.println(b.pi());
    wchntConsole.println(b.toConstruction(0, helper));
    wchntConsole.println(b.relabel("Eve", 9).toConstruction(0, helper));
}
```
